iFixit operates a community-powered platform hosting 100,000+ device repair guides and compatibility information, making repair knowledge accessible to billions globally. The platform combines professional technical documentation with crowdsourced repair insights and troubleshooting data. iFixit developed the Repairability Index (IOR) scoring system adopted by regulatory bodies and manufacturers, creating market incentives for design-for-repair. During COVID-19, iFixit processed 13,000 medical device repair manual PDFs enabling hospital technicians to maintain critical equipment. The platform demonstrates that democratized repair documentation reduces barriers to maintenance, extends product lifespans, and creates regulatory frameworks rewarding maintainability in product design.